Deferred. Do not start this without the trigger below; it is recorded so the
reasoning is not re-derived.

Priority is a project field today. The header earns its fixed positions by
answering "can I start this?" in two lines, and priority does not help with
that — it answers "which of these should I pick?", a sort over candidates
that have already survived the filter. That set is small, so reading past
each one's fields is cheap, and projects that do not want priority pay
nothing.

Trigger: picking among unblocked tickets turning out to need a sort that
reads every candidate's fields often enough to show up in a measurement. At
that point it becomes a fourth header line, not a fourth opinion — and note
that every structural line is a cost every ticket carries forever.

27 makes the counter-argument cheaper to test: one awk pass reads a field
across every ticket in 0.44s over 2000 of them, which is the measurement
this trigger asks for.
